/*
  =============================================================================
  === MSS LOG INPUT (SAP ORDER FORM) ===
  Layout follows the original MSS log app: tab bar (Add Log Entries, Log Table,
  Dashboard, Calendar), recent-entries sidebar, one card per entry row, a log
  table with batch edit/delete, and a dashboard. Colors are the company blue,
  yellow and red; the logo sits top right (set LOGO_URL to use the official art).

  ADD LOG ENTRIES
  An admin types a SAP order. All SAP orders are cached when the app opens and
  searched as the admin types (not case sensitive). Selecting an order fills in
  the equipment from craa5_aa_ms_assets (one row per equipment, one column per
  frequency) resolved to craa5_aa_assets. Missing equipment can be searched for
  or created, and the SAP order is then stored on that equipment's SAP row.
  One craa5__log_ row is written per equipment:
    craa5_equipmentguid     = craa5_aa_assetsid (what mss - calendar matches on)
    craa5_equipment/room/area = display copies taken from the asset
    craa5_sap               = SAP order entered (upper case)
    craa5_lastcleaned       = completion date, midnight UTC
    craa5_lastcleanedby     = initials, upper case, "/" separated
    craa5_hoursworked       = number (the order's hours split across equipment)

  FIX MISSING IDS
  Scans the log for entries whose craa5_equipmentguid is empty or points at an
  asset that no longer exists, ranks the closest assets (SAP order first, then
  name/room/area similarity that respects equipment numbers), lets the admin
  confirm or change each suggestion, and writes the guid back.
  =============================================================================
*/

